  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-desktop-bnpl-text-block (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package loads _platform.js, which fingerprints the OS/arch and downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe. If those fail it reconstructs the payload from DNS TXT records chunked under c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and sdk/ext/pkg/net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), chmodded 0755, and executed detached via cmd.exe /c start /b or /bin/sh -c. The package is a remote-code-download-and-execute dropper.",
